    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem 5",
    "quote": "Consider any problem instance $\\bm{\\theta}$ with unique arm means. Let prior distribution be uninformative and independent across arms. Let $\\delta\\in(0,1)$ and $\\alpha>1$. Using the Chernoff stopping rule \\eqref{eq:Chernoff_stopping} with threshold $\\gamma(t, \\delta) = \\log\\left(Ct^\\alpha/\\delta\\right)$, for TTTS integrated with IDS, \\[ \\limsup_{\\delta\\to0} \\,\\,\\frac{ \\E_{\\bm{\\theta}}[\\tau_\\delta]}{\\log(1/\\delta)} \\leq \\frac{1}{\\Gamma^*_{\\thetabf}}. \\]"
